    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac1P$, $P\\ne0$ and $S\\ne0$.\n\nFactorise the denominators and cancel $a+b$ after combining.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{a^2+ab}+\\frac1{b^2+ab}&=\\frac1{a(a+b)}+\\frac1{b(a+b)}\\\\\\frac1{a^2+ab}+\\frac1{b^2+ab}&=\\frac{a+b}{ab(a+b)}\\\\\\frac1{a^2+ab}+\\frac1{b^2+ab}&=\\frac1{ab}\\\\\\frac1{a^2+ab}+\\frac1{b^2+ab}&=\\frac1P\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: real $a,b$ with $a\\ne0$, $b\\ne0$ and $a+b\\ne0$. Thus $P=ab\\ne0$ and $S=a+b\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
